12] [SWS_EM_01309] [SWS_EM_01314] [SWS_EM_01401] [SWS_EM_01402] [SWS_EM_01403] [SWS_EM_01404] [SWS_EM_02000] [SWS_EM_02001] [SWS_EM_02002] [SWS_EM_02003] [SWS_EM_02243] [SWS_EM_02558] [SWS_EM_02560] [SWS_EM_02562] [SWS_EM_02563] [SWS_EM_02564] [SWS_EM_02565] [SWS_EM_02566] [SWS_EM_02567] [SWS_EM_02568] [SWS_EM_02577] [SWS_EM_02578] [SWS_EM_02579] [SWS_EM_02580] [SWS_EM_02581]","why":[{"c":0.95,"m":"cached_context_sweep/agy","mod":"gemini-3.8-flash","r":"Spezifikations-Zitat SWS_EM_02000 im Belegtext.","rel":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","rls":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"role":"constitutive","t":["SWS_EM_02000"]}]},{"confidence":0.95,"doc":"AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_ExecutionManagement","id":"SNIP_exec_AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_E_P36_106","is_figure":false,"page":36,"relation":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","targets":["SWS_EM_02281","SWS_EM_02290"],"text":"Specification of Execution Management AUTOSAR AP R23-11 Depending on the Machine State or on any other Function Group State , de- ployed Executables are started during AUTOSAR Adaptive Platform startup or later, however it is not expected that all will begin active work immediately since many processes will provide services to other processes and therefore wait and listen for incoming service requests. Execution Management derives an ordering for startup/shutdown of deployed Exe- cutables within the context of Machine and/or Function Group State changes based on declared Execution Dependencies [SWS_EM_01050]. The dependencies are described in the Execution Manifests , see [TPS_MANI_01041]. Execution Management is not responsible for run-time scheduling of processes since this is the responsibility of the Operating System [SWS_OSI_01003]. How- ever, Execution Management is responsible for initialization / configuration of the OS to enable it to perform the necessary run-time scheduling and resource manage- ment based on information extracted by Execution Management from the Machine Manifest and Execution Manifests . Execution Management does not perform standardized termination handling - the response to receipt of a signal, e.g. SIGTERM , by Execution Management is there- fore implementation defined. 7.3.1 Error handling All API operations can potentially raise errors. [SWS_EM_02547] Obtain error information ⌈ According to Adaptive Platform Core [4], Execution Management shall provide means to obtain information about errors that occurred during API calls. For that reason, Execution Management can return the following errors: • ara::exec::ExecErrc [SWS_EM_02281] • ara::exec::ExecException [SWS_EM_02282] • ara::exec::ExecException::ExecException [SWS_EM_02283] • ara::exec::ExecErrorDomain [SWS_EM_02284] • ara::exec::ExecErrorDomain::ExecErrorDomain [SWS_EM_02286] • ara::exec::ExecErrorDomain::Name [SWS_EM_02287] • ara::exec::ExecErrorDomain::Message [SWS_EM_02288] • ara::exec::GetExecErrorDomain [SWS_EM_02290] ⌋ (RS_EM_00150) 36 of 197 Document ID 721: AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_ExecutionManagement","why":[{"c":0.95,"m":"cached_context_sweep/agy","mod":"gemini-3.8-flash","r":"Spezifikations-Zitat SWS_EM_02281 im Belegtext.","rel":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","rls":["R23-11"],"role":"constitutive","t":["SWS_EM_02281"]},{"c":0.95,"m":"cached_context_sweep/agy","mod":"gemini-3.8-flash","r":"Spezifikations-Zitat SWS_EM_02290 im Belegtext.","rel":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","rls":["R23-11"],"role":"constitutive","t":["SWS_EM_02290"]}]},{"confidence":0.95,"doc":"AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_ExecutionManagement","id":"SNIP_exec_AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_E_P37_107","is_figure":false,"page":37,"relation":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","targets":["SWS_EM_02291"],"text":"Specification of Execution Management AUTOSAR AP R23-11 [SWS_EM_02548] Create error information ⌈ According to Adaptive Platform Core [4], Execution Management shall provide means to create error information as listed below. • ara::exec::ExecErrorDomain::ThrowAsException [SWS_EM_02289] • ara::exec::MakeErrorCode [SWS_EM_02291] ⌋ (RS_EM_00150) 37 of 197 Document ID 721: AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_ExecutionManagement","why":[{"c":0.95,"m":"cached_context_sweep/agy","mod":"gemini-3.8-flash","r":"Spezifikations-Zitat SWS_EM_02291 im Belegtext.","rel":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","rls":["R23-11"],"role":"constitutive","t":["SWS_EM_02291"]}]},{"confidence":0.95,"doc":"AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_ExecutionManagement","id":"SNIP_exec_AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_E_P38_108","is_figure":false,"page":38,"relation":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","targets":["SWS_EM_02000"],"text":"Specification of Execution Management AUTOSAR AP R23-11 7.4 Process Lifecycle Management 7.4.1 Execution State Execution States characterizes the internal lifecycle of a process . In other words, they describe it from the point of view of a process that is executed. The states visible to the process are defined by the ara::exec::ExecutionState enumeration, see [SWS_EM_02000].","why":[{"c":0.95,"m":"cached_context_sweep/agy","mod":"gemini-3.8-flash","r":"Spezifikations-Zitat SWS_EM_02000 im Belegtext.","rel":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","rls":["R23-11"],"role":"constitutive","t":["SWS_EM_02000"]}]},{"confidence":0.9,"doc":"AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_ExecutionManagement","id":"FIG-5098beb0f17bc056","is_figure":true,"page":32,"relation":"heuristic","targets":["SWS_EM_02000"],"text":"Figure 7.2: Execution States","why":[{"c":0.9,"m":"cached_context_sweep/agy","mod":"gemini-3.8-flash","r":"ExecutionState enum and internal states","role":"heuristic","t":["SWS_EM_02000"]}]},{"confidence":0.9,"doc":"AUTOSAR_EXP_PlatformDesign","id":"FIG-5b942f9084b65a92","is_figure":true,"page":29,"relation":"heuristic","targets":["SWS_EM_02000"],"text":"Figure 5: 3 Interaction between States","why":[{"c":0.9,"m":"cached_context_sweep/agy","mod":"gemini-3.8-flash","r":"ExecutionState enumeration for processes","role":"heuristic","t":["SWS_EM_02000"]}]},{"confidence":0.9,"doc":"AUTOSAR_SWS_ExecutionManagement","id":"FIG-dbbf6bdbe0346f09","is_figure":true,"page":29,"relation":"heuristic","targets":["SWS_EM_02000"],"text":"Figure 7.5: Application States","why":[{"c":0.9,"m":"cached_context_sweep/agy","mod":"gemini-3.8-flash","r":"Process internal ExecutionState definition","role":"heuristic","t":["SWS_EM_02000"]}]},{"confidence":0.9,"doc":"AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_ExecutionManagement","id":"SNIP_exec_AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_E_P115_202","is_figure":false,"page":115,"relation":"heuristic","targets":["SWS_EM_02000"],"text":"⌋ (RS_EM_00103, RS_AP_00134) Please note that ExecutionState includes only states reportable by the process to Execution Management and therefore does not include enumerations e.g. the \"Ini- tializing\" state mentioned in figure 7.3 and 7.13, which are an implied states for Exe- cution Management . The Initializing state starts when process is first scheduled (so no code executed yet) and ends when kRunning is reported ([SWS_EM_01004]). The Terminating state starts when termination is requested by Execution Manage- ment and ends when the process terminates ([SWS_EM_01404]). For the reasons mentioned, Execution Management assumes that process is in initializing state until kRunning will be reported by it. 8.1.2 ActivationReturnType [SWS_EM_02201] {OBSOLETE} Definition of API enum ara::exec::ActivationRe- turnType ⌈","why":[{"c":0.9,"m":"cached_context_sweep/agy","mod":"gemini-3.8-flash","r":"Explains ExecutionState reportable enum states.","role":"heuristic","t":["SWS_EM_02000"]}]},{"confidence":0.9,"doc":"AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_ExecutionManagement","id":"SNIP_exec_AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_E_P128_273","is_figure":false,"page":128,"relation":"heuristic","targets":["SWS_EM_02281"],"text":"ara::exec::ExecErrc::k CycleOverrun","why":[{"c":0.9,"m":"cached_context_sweep/agy","mod":"gemini-3.8-flash","r":"ExecErrc enum error codes","role":"heuristic","t":["SWS_EM_02281"]}]},{"confidence":0.9,"doc":"AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_ExecutionManagement","id":"SNIP_exec_AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_E_P130_284","is_figure":false,"page":130,"relation":"heuristic","targets":["SWS_EM_02281"],"text":"ara::exec::ExecErrc::kNo TimeStamp","why":[{"c":0.9,"m":"cached_context_sweep/agy","mod":"gemini-3.8-flash","r